          {
            "count": 3,
            "bug_id": 19334,
            "text": "Created attachment 4093\npatch v2: compare argument tags as symbols in exact matches (also c(), na.rm, UseMethod, NextMethod)\n\nI've extended the patch to the other places that match a tag exactly against a known name: `c()` and `unlist()` looking for `recursive` and `use.names`, the `na.rm` lookup in `sum()`, `max()`, `any()` and friends, the dispatch argument in `UseMethod()`, and `NextMethod()` re-matching its arguments. These used `pmatch()`, which translates names whose encoding marks differ, but a symbol name only keeps a mark in the locale's own encoding, so comparing the symbols gives the same answer.\n\nWith it, `c(a = x, b = y)` executes 6.7% fewer instructions, `c(x, y, recursive = TRUE)` 3.7% and a call through `NextMethod()` 2.3%. The new patch (against r90922) replaces attachment 4091, and the extended benchmark replaces 4092. `make check` passes on macOS; patch also at https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/503.",
